BUF-1 implemented: receive takes &mut BufReader<R> with R: Read + AsRawFd. Inspect buffered data first; scan at most the remaining frame allowance, append only payload strictly below MAX_FRAME, consume only through the first newline. Wait on get_ref().as_raw_fd() only with an empty buffer, then fill_buf. Preserve unique_json before typed decoding, duplicate rejection, EOF/protocol errors and transient WouldBlock/Interrupted retries.
BUF-1 evidence: 09-test-1.log. Deterministic counted real reads from anonymous Linux memfd; realistic 32KiB payload containing all byte values serializes to 117101 bytes. Capacities 1024/8192/32768 take exactly 115/15/4 underlying reads, respectively (ceil(wire_bytes/capacity)). This measures read scaling, not end-to-end elapsed time or live-job attribution. Boundary cases cover MAX_FRAME-1/MAX_FRAME/MAX_FRAME+1 with/without newline and capacities 17/8192/MAX_FRAME+32. Malformed, escaped/root/nested duplicate, unknown-field/type, invalid typed fields/bytes, empty/truncated/missing-newline EOF and fatal IO remain Protocol.

BUF-2 implemented: cancellation and original deadline checked on every receive iteration, including buffered data and after refill. Worker stdin wrapped once before Initialize and moved unchanged into demux; host stdout wrapped once before its receive loop. The host post-Reply EOF check also honors buffered overread before polling and preserves trailing-byte rejection and shutdown errors.
BUF-2 evidence: 09-test-1/2/3.log. Coalesced frames with live empty sockets; Initialize-to-demux buffered ResponseStart/ResponseChunk sequence 0; original sequence-0 fragmented response regression; buffered cancellation/deadline without consumption, cancellation between prefixes, empty-socket wait cancellation/deadline; three-byte reads with WouldBlock and Interrupted before/after partial progress; buffered trailing post-Reply data rejected without waiting for EOF.

